# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output
out/
dist/
dist-mcp/
dist-test/
release/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Native rebuilds
electron-builder/
build/unpacked/

# Everything under vendor/ is fetched by scripts/fetch-addons.mjs: the two
# executables are 200 MB between them, the licence text is copied out of the same
# archive, and the download cache holds a further ~110 MB. Committing any of it
# makes the repo uncloneable, and every byte of it is available from the vendor
# with a checksum. Run `npm run addons` after cloning; `npm run package` does it
# for you.
vendor/

# Environment and secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx

# Logs and caches
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.npm/
.cache/
.vite/

# Local GUI probe output (screenshots + report); the harness, not its runs.
probe/

# Working notes, not documentation.
#
# Plans are how the work gets thought through, and they go stale the moment the
# work lands. The UI overhaul plan sat in the tree for a full implementation
# cycle describing a UI that now exists, and nothing referenced it - so it read
# as current documentation while being nothing of the kind. Anything that helps
# decide what to build belongs in the commit message or an issue, not here.
*-plan.md
*-plans.md
*-notes.md
PLAN.md
NOTES.md
TODO.md
SCRATCH.md
*.scratch.md

# The same, uppercase. `.gitignore` matching is case-sensitive, and a plan
# written as SHOUTING-NAME.md is still a plan - one of these was called
# OPENPICS_FIX_PLAN.md and sat untracked in status forever because the rule
# above only covered lowercase.
*[-_]PLAN.md
*[-_]PLAN*.md
*[-_]NOTES*.md
*[-_]TODO*.md

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej

